    browser_handler tryMemoryProgramGap
    admits_on memory_program_reading
    because "issue 1175 R3: a memory program gap claims only when the request reads as a seeded program family"
  claim_note "Issue 1175 R3 follow-up round: a handler that used to answer without its input now records a named refusal event in that branch, so its row admits on the input and keeps the no-input answer through the refusal lane; the assistant itself is the subject of a question that addresses it or names no other subject."
  claim
    handler conversation_control
    admits_on backticked_term
    admits_on prior_reply
    refusal_event "conversation_control:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: a preference claims with the backticked term it avoids and a correction with the earlier action it corrects; a correction with no earlier turn is admitted to the refusal lane"
  claim
    handler agentic_continuation
    browser_handler tryAgenticContinuation
    admits_on prior_reply
    refusal_event "agentic_continuation:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: a continuation claims with the earlier task it resumes; with nothing to resume it is admitted to the refusal lane"
  claim
    handler clarification
    browser_handler tryClarification
    admits_on prior_reply
    refusal_event "clarification:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: a clarification request claims with the earlier reply it asks about; with none it is admitted to the refusal lane"
  claim
    handler current_dialogue_fact_checking
    browser_handler tryCurrentDialogueFactChecking
    admits_on prior_user_request
    refusal_event "current_dialogue_fact_checking:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: a dialogue fact check claims with the earlier statements it checks; with none it is admitted to the refusal lane"
  claim
    handler historical
    browser_handler tryHistorical
    admits_on dialogue_turn
    admits_on name_assignment
    refusal_event "conversation_recall:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: a recap or recall claims with the earlier turns it reads, a naming with the name it assigns; a recall with no earlier message is admitted to the refusal lane"
  claim
    handler conversation_memory
    admits_on dialogue_turn
    admits_on name_assignment
    admits_on recall_query_term
    admits_on supplied_payload
    refusal_event "conversation_recall:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: a conversation recall claims with the earlier turns, the name it assigns, the term it recalls or the text it summarizes; a request with none of them is admitted to the refusal lane"
  claim
    handler summarization
    admits_on summary_topic
    refusal_event "summarization:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: a topic summary claims with the seeded topic it summarizes; any other topic is admitted to the refusal lane"
  claim
    handler brainstorming
    browser_handler tryBrainstormingRequest
    admits_on brainstorm_category
    refusal_event "brainstorming:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: a brainstorm list claims with the category its keywords name; the default category is admitted to the refusal lane"
  claim
    handler roleplay
    browser_handler tryRoleplayRequest
    admits_on persona_or_topic
    refusal_event "roleplay:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: a roleplay claims with the persona or topic it names; the default persona on the fallback topic is admitted to the refusal lane"
  claim
    handler document_originality_check
    browser_handler tryDocumentOriginalityCheck
    admits_on document_operand
    refusal_event "document_originality_check:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: an originality check claims with the document it checks, an attachment, a text sample or a supplied text; a named but unsupplied document is admitted to the refusal lane"
  claim
    handler translation
    browser_handler tryTranslation
    admits_on translation_text
    refusal_event "translation:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: a translation claims with the text it translates; a request with no source phrase is admitted to the refusal lane"
  claim
    handler triz_resolution
    browser_handler tryTrizResolution
    admits_on triz_precedent
    refusal_event "triz_resolution:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: a contradiction question claims with the precedent its words overlap; with none it is admitted to the refusal lane"
  claim
    handler algorithm
    browser_handler tryAlgorithm
    admits_on algorithm_operation
    refusal_event "algorithm:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: an algorithm request claims with the operation it names; with none it is admitted to the refusal lane"
  claim
    handler source_refresh
    browser_handler trySourceRefresh
    admits_on source_reference
    refusal_event "source_refresh:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: a refresh claims with the source it names, a URL or a path; with none it is admitted to the refusal lane"
  claim
    handler proof_request
    browser_handler tryProofRequest
    admits_on stated_claim
    refusal_event "proof_request:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: a proof request claims with the claim it states beyond its directive; with none it is admitted to the refusal lane"
  claim
    handler capabilities
    browser_handler tryCapabilities
    admits_on assistant_subject
    because "issue 1175 R3: a capability question claims only when its subject is the assistant, addressed or left unnamed, never when it names another subject"
  claim
    handler meta_explanation
    browser_handler tryMetaExplanation
    admits_on assistant_subject
    because "issue 1175 R3: a question about how or why the assistant answers claims only when its subject is the assistant, addressed or left unnamed"
  claim
    handler network_query
    browser_handler tryNetworkSnapshot
    admits_on assistant_subject
    because "issue 1175 R3: a network question claims only when its subject is the assistant's own network, addressed or left unnamed"
  claim
    handler exact_memory_query
    browser_handler tryExactMemoryQuery
    admits_on memory_query_statement
    because "issue 1175 R3: an exact memory query claims only with a statement in a memory query dialect"
  claim
    handler fact_lookup
    admits_on fact_subject
    because "issue 1175 R3: a fact question claims only with the subject one of its arms resolves: a question over supplied text, a comparison of seeded subjects, the gated record, a live relation and subject, or the concept an explanation researches"
  claim_note "Issue 1175 R3 last five rows: each handler that read nothing but its cue now reads the operand its answer is about, through a reader the rule interpreter also captures the operand with (value <name> operand <kind>), so the row and the answer read the same thing."
  claim
    handler docs_method_explanation
    browser_handler tryDocsMethodExplanation
    admits_on documented_method
    because "issue 1175 R3: a documentation explanation claims only when the prompt names the project and the method of a seeded documentation page, never on an explanation lead alone"
  claim
    handler kupi_slona
    browser_handler tryKupiSlona
    admits_on idiom_utterance
    because "issue 1175 R3: the circular idiom claims only when it is the whole utterance, framed at most by particles and function words, never when the phrase merely occurs inside another request"
  claim
    handler source_conflict
    browser_handler trySourceConflict
    admits_on attributed_alternatives
    refusal_event "source_conflict:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: a source conflict claims an answer only with the two alternatives it attributes to sources, and names them; a cued conflict without them is admitted to the refusal lane"
  claim
    handler github_repository_traffic
    browser_handler tryGithubRepositoryTraffic
    admits_on named_repository
    refusal_event "github_repository_traffic:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: a traffic answer names a repository only when the prompt names it, as an owner/name slug or URL or as the assistant's own; a question about an unnamed repository is admitted to the refusal lane, which states the policy for any repository"
  claim
    handler formalization_request
    browser_handler tryFormalizationRequest
    admits_on formalization_statement
    refusal_event "formalization_request:refusal"
    because "issue 1175 R3: a formalization claims only with a statement beyond its cue, or the formal clause a deformalization reads; a cue without one is admitted to the refusal lane"
